1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:04,340
Before you walk out that door
today, give me a few minutes.

2
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,760
You already know what's out there.

3
00:00:07,070 --> 00:00:08,780
The email you've been dreading.

4
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,540
The drive.

5
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:13,360
The conversation you keep putting off.

6
00:00:13,690 --> 00:00:17,890
And you're about to walk into all
of it with nothing between you

7
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:20,190
and the day but a cup of coffee.

8
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:23,640
This psalm is for the person
standing at that door.

9
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,840
People have prayed it in
hospital hallways, before shifts,

10
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:31,780
and on the way to jobs
they were scared to lose.

11
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:34,760
Pray it with me, and then go.

12
00:00:36,657 --> 00:00:38,607
Here is how it starts.

13
00:00:38,967 --> 00:00:41,877
Psalm 91, verses 1 and 2.

14
00:00:43,807 --> 00:00:48,084
He that dwelleth in the secret
place of the most High shall

15
00:00:48,084 --> 00:00:52,652
abide under the shadow of the
Almighty. I will say of the LORD,

16
00:00:52,652 --> 00:00:57,074
He is my refuge and my fortress:
my God; in him will I trust.

17
00:00:59,237 --> 00:01:01,037
Look at the word dwelleth.

18
00:01:01,397 --> 00:01:03,497
That's somebody who lives there.

19
00:01:03,857 --> 00:01:07,577
Not a person who stops by
when the car breaks down.

20
00:01:07,927 --> 00:01:10,517
This one is for an ordinary Tuesday,

21
00:01:10,517 --> 00:01:14,107
when nobody is watching
and nothing is on fire.

22
00:01:14,457 --> 00:01:17,877
When's the last time you prayed
before you left the house,

23
00:01:17,877 --> 00:01:20,317
instead of after something went wrong?

24
00:01:21,797 --> 00:01:24,727
And look at what the
writer does in verse 2.

25
00:01:25,087 --> 00:01:26,887
He says it out loud.

26
00:01:27,247 --> 00:01:29,177
I will say of the LORD.

27
00:01:29,527 --> 00:01:32,077
Your worry talks all morning long.

28
00:01:32,437 --> 00:01:34,317
Faith has to talk back.

29
00:01:36,490 --> 00:01:38,310
Verses 3 and 4.

30
00:01:40,248 --> 00:01:44,835
Surely he shall deliver thee from
the snare of the fowler, and from the

31
00:01:44,835 --> 00:01:49,228
noisome pestilence. He shall cover
thee with his feathers, and under

32
00:01:49,228 --> 00:01:53,750
his wings shalt thou trust: his truth
shall be thy shield and buckler.

33
00:01:55,910 --> 00:01:57,460
A fowler is a trapper,

34
00:01:57,460 --> 00:02:00,850
and a snare is the trap
you never saw coming.

35
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,620
The bad deal.

36
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:04,480
The wrong crowd.

37
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,940
The text you should not have sent.

38
00:02:07,290 --> 00:02:10,670
God sees the trap before
you ever step toward it.

39
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,380
Then comes the picture I love.

40
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:16,310
Under his wings.

41
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:20,620
A mother bird covers her young
with her own body when the weather

42
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:24,420
turns, and whatever is coming
has to get through her first.

43
00:02:26,590 --> 00:02:28,480
Verses 5 through 8.

44
00:02:30,412 --> 00:02:35,311
Thou shalt not be afraid for the
terror by night; nor for the arrow that

45
00:02:35,311 --> 00:02:40,142
flieth by day; Nor for the pestilence
that walketh in darkness; nor for

46
00:02:40,142 --> 00:02:45,245
the destruction that wasteth at noonday.
A thousand shall fall at thy side,

47
00:02:45,245 --> 00:02:49,872
and ten thousand at thy right hand;
but it shall not come nigh thee.

48
00:02:49,872 --> 00:02:54,771
Only with thine eyes shalt thou behold
and see the reward of the wicked.

49
00:02:56,930 --> 00:03:01,140
Four hours are named in there,
the night, the day, the darkness,

50
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:01,930
and noon.

51
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:05,860
There is no hour on the clock
that was left uncovered.

52
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:10,050
The fear that hits at three in
the morning is on that list,

53
00:03:10,050 --> 00:03:13,760
and so is the trouble that
shows up in broad daylight.

54
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:19,150
So does that mean nothing bad
ever comes near a believer?

55
00:03:19,510 --> 00:03:21,080
Read it again.

56
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:24,150
It never says nothing will come at you.

57
00:03:24,510 --> 00:03:27,380
It says you do not have
to be afraid of it.

58
00:03:27,730 --> 00:03:33,520
Jesus said the same thing plainly,
in John chapter 16, verse 33.

59
00:03:35,449 --> 00:03:40,931
These things I have spoken unto you, that
in me ye might have peace. In the world

60
00:03:40,931 --> 00:03:46,007
ye shall have tribulation: but be of
good cheer; I have overcome the world.

61
00:03:48,863 --> 00:03:50,453
Back to the psalm.

62
00:03:50,803 --> 00:03:52,583
Verses 9 and 10.

63
00:03:54,522 --> 00:03:58,510
Because thou hast made the
LORD, which is my refuge, even

64
00:03:58,510 --> 00:04:02,497
the most High, thy habitation;
There shall no evil befall

65
00:04:02,497 --> 00:04:06,275
thee, neither shall any
plague come nigh thy dwelling.

66
00:04:08,433 --> 00:04:10,083
Thy habitation.

67
00:04:10,443 --> 00:04:12,963
It keeps coming back to where you live.

68
00:04:13,323 --> 00:04:17,263
Proverbs chapter 18, verse
10 puts it another way.

69
00:04:19,192 --> 00:04:22,021
The name of the LORD
is a strong tower: the

70
00:04:22,021 --> 00:04:24,588
righteous runneth into it, and is safe.

71
00:04:26,753 --> 00:04:28,253
Runneth into it.

72
00:04:28,613 --> 00:04:30,753
So when the fear comes, run.

73
00:04:31,113 --> 00:04:32,503
Say his name.

74
00:04:32,863 --> 00:04:34,813
You don't need fancy words.

75
00:04:35,173 --> 00:04:37,883
Jesus, help me, is a whole prayer.

76
00:04:40,057 --> 00:04:42,217
Verses 11 through 13.

77
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:48,597
For he shall give his angels charge
over thee, to keep thee in all

78
00:04:48,597 --> 00:04:52,899
thy ways. They shall bear thee
up in their hands, lest thou dash

79
00:04:52,899 --> 00:04:56,933
thy foot against a stone. Thou
shalt tread upon the lion and

80
00:04:56,933 --> 00:05:01,437
adder: the young lion and the dragon
shalt thou trample under feet.

81
00:05:03,597 --> 00:05:05,417
You have help you can't see.

82
00:05:05,777 --> 00:05:08,707
God gives his angels orders about you.

83
00:05:09,067 --> 00:05:12,827
How many close calls have
you already walked away from?

84
00:05:13,187 --> 00:05:17,267
You have probably been kept from
things you will never hear about.

85
00:05:17,627 --> 00:05:19,977
The truck that did not cross the line.

86
00:05:20,337 --> 00:05:24,117
The night you made it home when
you had no business making it.

87
00:05:25,607 --> 00:05:27,297
One careful note.

88
00:05:27,657 --> 00:05:30,877
The devil set Jesus on
the top of the temple,

89
00:05:30,877 --> 00:05:34,507
quoted these very verses,
and dared him to jump.

90
00:05:34,867 --> 00:05:36,497
Jesus said no.

91
00:05:36,857 --> 00:05:40,577
This psalm is a shelter for
people who walk with God.

92
00:05:40,937 --> 00:05:44,677
It was never a permission
slip to go looking for danger.

93
00:05:46,857 --> 00:05:50,747
Now listen, because in
verse 14 the voice changes.

94
00:05:51,107 --> 00:05:53,507
God himself starts to talk.

95
00:05:53,867 --> 00:05:56,157
Verses 14 through 16.

96
00:05:58,081 --> 00:06:02,880
Because he hath set his love upon me,
therefore will I deliver him: I will

97
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:07,680
set him on high, because he hath known
my name. He shall call upon me, and

98
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:12,415
I will answer him: I will be with him
in trouble; I will deliver him, and

99
00:06:12,415 --> 00:06:17,150
honour him. With long life will I
satisfy him, and shew him my salvation.

100
00:06:19,317 --> 00:06:21,077
Look at the middle of that.

101
00:06:21,437 --> 00:06:23,637
I will be with him in trouble.

102
00:06:23,997 --> 00:06:27,287
He never said you would
not see trouble today.

103
00:06:27,647 --> 00:06:30,127
He said you would not be in it alone.

104
00:06:31,617 --> 00:06:33,247
And look at the reason.

105
00:06:33,597 --> 00:06:35,887
Because he hath set his love upon me.

106
00:06:36,247 --> 00:06:40,417
This whole psalm rests on a
relationship, not a formula.

107
00:06:40,777 --> 00:06:45,217
If you have drifted, this morning
is a good morning to walk back.

108
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,190
So here is the prayer.

109
00:06:48,490 --> 00:06:50,560
Pray it out loud if you can.

110
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:54,020
Father, I am stepping out the door,

111
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:58,020
and I am putting this day under Your wing.

112
00:06:58,330 --> 00:07:00,640
Cover my house while I am gone.

113
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:05,300
Cover the ones I love,
wherever they are, right now.

114
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:09,120
When a trap is set, show me before I step.

115
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:12,780
When fear comes, remind me where I dwell.

116
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,580
Send your angels ahead of me,

117
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:20,130
and let me come home tonight
with a thankful heart.

118
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:24,400
I ask it in the name
of Jesus Christ, Amen.

119
00:07:25,050 --> 00:07:28,200
Type, amen, and send this
to a friend who needs it.

120
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:31,650
Have a blessed day and
remember the word for today.

